eline - Conf Call', 'text': 'ANTHEM SAYS JUNE EXPERIENCE, WHILE STILL EARLY, SUGGESTS THAT HEALTHCARE UTILIZATION RECOVERED TO ROUGHLY 90% OF BASELINE- CONF CALL.ANTHEM EXPECTS INCREASED HEALTHCARE UTILIZATION TRENDS TO INCREASE MEDICAL LOSS RATIO BY A COUPLE HUNDRED BASIS POINTS IN 2H 2020 - CONF CALL.ANTHEM CEO EXPECTS TO LOSE MORE COMMERCIAL LIVES AS UNEMPLOYMENT CONTINUES - CONF CALL.ANTHEM SAYS INGENIORX NEW PRESCRIPTIONS FELL 10% TO 15% IN APRIL VERSUS YEAR EARLIER- CONF CALL.'}{'symbol': 'ADP', 'date': '2020-07-29 09:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'ADP Reports Qtrly Adjusted Earnings Per Share $1.14', 'text': 'ADP REPORTS FOURTH QUARTER FISCAL 2020 RESULTS.QTRLY  REVENUES DECREASED 3% TO $3.4 BILLION.QTRLY  EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.96.QTRLY  ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.14.Q4 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $0.96, REVENUE VIEW $3.29 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.SEES 2021 REVENUE DECLINE OF 1% TO 4%.SEES 2021 DILUTED EPS DECLINE OF 12% TO 17%.SEES 2021 ADJUSTED DILUTED EPS DECLINE OF 13% TO 18%.SEES 2020 PRE-TAX CHARGES OF ABOUT $77 MILLION RELATED TO TRANSFORMATION INITIATIVES.SEES FISCAL 2021 PRE-TAX CHARGES OF ABOUT $60 MILLION RELATED TO TRANSFORMATION INITIATIVES.SEES 2021 EMPLOYER SERVICES REVENUE DECLINE OF 3% TO 5%.SEES 2021 PEO SERVICES REVENUE DECLINE OF 2% TO GROWTH OF 2%.'}{'symbol': 'BAX', 'date': '2020-07-29 10:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Baxter And Ayogo Announce Partnership For Digital Health Solutions For Home Dialysis', 'text': 'BAXTER AND AYOGO ANNOUNCE PARTNERSHIP FOR UNIQUE DIGITAL HEALTH SOLUTIONS FOR HOME DIALYSIS.BAXTER AND AYOGO ANNOUNCE PARTNERSHIP FOR UNIQUE DIGITAL HEALTH SOLUTIONS FOR HOME DIALYSIS.BAXTER INTERNATIONAL INC - FINANCIAL DETAILS OF AGREEMENT WERE NOT DISCLOSED.BAXTER INTERNATIONAL - ALSO MADE AN EQUITY INVESTMENT IN AYOGO IN EXCHANGE FOR MINORITY INTEREST IN CO.'}{'symbol': 'BA', 'date': '2020-07-29 15:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Boeing CEO Envisages The 787 Will Return To Build Rate Of 10-11/Month At Some Point', 'text': 'ON QUESTION OF SPACE AT EVERETT PLANT OPENED BY 747 DEMISE AND POTENTIAL 787 CONSOLIDATION, BOEING CEO SAYS CO IS AT THE "FRONT END" OF THAT EVALUATION.BOEING CEO SAYS ENVISAGES THAT BOEING 787 WILL RETURN TO BUILD RATE OF 10-11 PER MONTH AT SOME POINT.BOEING CEO SAYS DON’T HAVE A POINT OF VIEW WITH RESPECT TO THE U.S. ELECTIONS.BOEING CFO SAYS CO FACILITATING ACCESS FOR SUPPLIERS TO CARES ACT FUNDING, FOCUSED ON KEEPING SUPPLY CHAIN HEALTHY.BOEING CEO SAYS 737 MAX RECERTIFICATION PROCESS HAS BEEN TRANSPARENT AND CONSTRUCTIVE.BOEING CEO SAYS COVID-19 HAS ELONGATED 737 MAX RECERTIFICATION.'}{'symbol': 'BA', 'date': '2020-07-29 13:30:00-04:56', 'title': "Boeing Says 737 MAX's Return Would Be The Main Driver Of Positive Cash Flow In 2021 - Conf Call", 'text': 'BOEING CEO SAYS MODIFYING WORK AREAS TO ALLOW FOR PHYSICAL DISTANCING - CONF CALL.BOEING CEO SAYS AIRLINES ARE DEFERRING AIRPLANE ORDERS, POSTPONING ACCEPTANCE OF COMPLETING ORDERS AND SLOWING DOWN OR STOPPING PAYMENTS; THEY ARE ALSO ACCELERATING AIRCRAFT RETIREMENTS.BOEING CEO SAYS CONTINUING PAYMENTS TO MORE THAN 12,000 SUPPLIERS.BOEING CEO SAYS WORKING CLOSELY WITH THE FAA AND GLOBAL REGULATORS TO GET THE 737 MAX BACK IN THE AIR.BOEING CEO SAYS OVERALL ENVIRONMENT DUE TO COVID-19 PRESENTS LOGISTICAL CHALLENGES FOR THE NECESSARY INTERNATIONAL TRAVEL AND THE IN PERSON MEETINGS, WHICH ARE REQUIRED FOR THE 737 MAX CERTIFICATION PROCESS.BOEING CEO SAYS NOW EXPECT THE NECESSARY REGULATORY APPROVALS FOR THE 737 MAX TO BE OBTAINED IN TIME TO SUPPORT RESUMPTION OF DELIVERIES IN Q4, 2020.BOEING CEO SAYS ENCOURAGED BY EARLY SIGNS OF PASSENGER TRAFFIC RECOVERY, BUT THE TRAJECTORY MAY BE UNEVEN GOING FORWARD.BOEING CEO SAYS U.S. AIR TRAVEL HAS SEEN SIGNS OF FLATTENING OR SLIGHT DECLINES IN JULY DUE TO A RISE IN COVID-19 CASES.BOEING CEO SAYS EXPECTS IT WILL TAKE THREE YEARS FOR TRAVEL TO RECOVER TO 2019 LEVELS, AND FEW YEARS BEYOND THAT FOR THE INDUSTRY TO RETURN TO NORMAL GROWTH TRENDS.BOEING CEO SAYS SO FAR HAS TRACKED RETIREMENTS OF CLOSE TO 1,000 OF THE MORE THAN 2,500 AIRCRAFT WITH 20-PLUS YEARS OF SERVICE PRIOR TO THE CRISIS.BOEING CEO SAYS EXPECTS MULTI-YEAR RECOVERY PERIOD FOR COMMERCIAL SERVICES BUSINESS.'}{'symbol': 'BA', 'date': '2020-07-29 11:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Aercap Continuing To Collect Cash From "Majority" Of Airline Customers - CEO', 'text': 'AIRCRAFT LESSOR AERCAP\'S CEO KELLY SAYS "WE HAVE BEGUN LEASING AIRPLANES AGAIN".AERCAP CEO - SURGE IN AIRCRAFT RETIREMENTS FOCUSED ON MODELS REPRESENTING LESS THAN 1% OF ITS FLEET.AERCAP CONTINUING TO COLLECT CASH FROM "MAJORITY" OF AIRLINE CUSTOMERS - CEO.'}{'symbol': 'BA', 'date': '2020-07-29 09:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Boeing Co Says Delaying Ramp Up Plans On 737 Production', 'text': 'BOEING CO SAYS CUTTING PRODUCTION ON 787,777 PROGRAMS.BOEING CO SAYS DELAYING ENTRY INTO SERVICE OF 777X TWINJET.BOEING CO ANNOUNCES END OF ICONIC 747 JET PROGRAM.BOEING CO SAYS DELAYING RAMP UP PLANS ON 737 PRODUCTION.BOEING CO SAYS DOES NOT SEE NEED TO RAISE ADDITIONAL MONEY IN DEBT MARKETS AT THIS TIME, KEEPING OPTIONS OPEN.BOEING CO SAYS BOOKED SEVERANCE COSTS IN QUARTER RELATED TO STAFF CUTS.BOEING CO SAYS HAS CLOSE TO $10 BILLION UNTAPPED CREDIT.BOEING CO SAYS BOOKED COSTS RELATED TO 737 MAX GROUNDING.'}{'symbol': 'BXP', 'date': '2020-07-29 20:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Boston Properties Reports July Office Tenant Collections Of 98%', 'text': 'BOSTON PROPERTIES ANNOUNCES SECOND QUARTER 2020 RESULTS; REPORTS EPS OF $1.71 AND FFO PER SHARE OF $1.52.Q2 FFO PER SHARE $1.52.SIGNS 942,000 SQUARE FEET OF LEASING IN Q2.REPORTS JULY OFFICE TENANT COLLECTIONS OF 98%.Q2 FFO PER SHARE VIEW $1.73 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.QTRLY TOTAL REVENUE $654.8 MILLION VERSUS $733.7 MILLION.Q2 REVENUE VIEW $724.4 MILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.'}{'symbol': 'CHRW', 'date': '2020-07-29 19:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Ch Robinson Worldwide Q2 Earnings Per Share $1.06', 'text': 'C.H. ROBINSON REPORTS 2020 SECOND QUARTER RESULTS.Q2 EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.06.Q2 REVENUE $3.6 BILLION VERSUS REFIN